Package: CDREGM
Title: Capitalism, Democracy and Rule of Law Economic Growth Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Cesar", "Garcia", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "gypsaman@gmail.com"),
    person("Felipe", "Llaugel", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Tools for estimating, extending, and visualising the
    Capitalism, Democracy, and Rule of Law (CDR) economic growth model of
    Ridley and Khan (2018) and Ridley and Llaugel (2018), in which three
    standardised institutional variables and their interaction explain
    cross-country growth. Provides the ordinary least squares and
    two-stage least squares estimators, the composite CDR index, the
    parametric endogenous growth rate, and a wide range of downstream
    analyses: bootstrap and robustness checks, panel and dynamic-panel
    models, quantile and Bayesian regression, spatial dependence tests,
    counterfactual policy simulation, reform-path optimisation, country
    reports, and an interactive explorer. A bundled 79-country panel of
    World Bank and V-Dem indicators supports out-of-the-box use, with
    helpers to refresh or extend it.
